# Third-Party Software and Reference Notice

The MIT License above applies to the original source code of
`pyside6-webusb`.

Third-party software, specifications, data, and reference implementations
remain subject to their respective copyrights and licenses.

Nothing in this notice relicenses third-party material under the MIT License.

## 1. Incorporated or Derived Material

### 1.1 Chromium USB Blocklist Data

The USB security hardening implementation contains VID/PID data derived from
Chromium's USB blocklist.

The corresponding Chromium source was reviewed during the project's license
audit, and the relevant VID/PID entries were compared against Chromium's
`usb_blocklist.cc`.

The applicable Chromium source is distributed under Chromium's BSD-style
licensing terms.

SPDX identifier:

`BSD-3-Clause`

Chromium License:

https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/HEAD/LICENSE

Chromium source:

https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/

The Chromium-derived data is limited to the relevant USB blocklist entries.
The surrounding Python implementation is independently implemented and is
licensed under the MIT License stated above.

### 1.2 W3C / WICG WebUSB WebIDL

The TypeScript WebUSB definitions include WebIDL material derived from the
WICG WebUSB specification.

WebUSB specification:

https://wicg.github.io/webusb/

W3C Software and Document License:

https://www.w3.org/copyright/software-license-2023/

The W3C-derived specification material remains subject to the applicable W3C
license.

The independently written TypeScript implementation surrounding the
specification-derived definitions remains subject to the MIT License stated
above, to the extent permitted by applicable law and license terms.

