# 2. Runtime Dependencies

The following software is used as external runtime or build dependencies.

They are not relicensed under the MIT License of `pyside6-webusb`.

## 2.1 Qt / PySide6 / QtWebEngine / Qt WebChannel

`pyside6-webusb` uses Qt and PySide6 APIs, including QtWebEngine and
Qt WebChannel.

The Qt WebChannel JavaScript implementation is obtained at runtime from the
Qt resource:

    :/qtwebchannel/qwebchannel.js

`qwebchannel.js` is not bundled as an independent copy of the Qt source in
this project.

The applicable license of the runtime-provided Qt component is determined by
the exact Qt/PySide6 distribution used by the host application.

Qt licensing:

https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/licensing.html

Qt third-party licenses:

https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/licenses-used-in-qt.html

This project does not make an independent blanket licensing assertion for
the runtime-provided Qt resource.

## 2.2 pyusb

`pyusb` is used as an external Python dependency for USB communication.

Project:

https://github.com/pyusb/pyusb

`pyusb` retains its own copyright and license.

## 2.3 libusb

`libusb` may be used as the native USB backend.

`libusb` is an external dependency and retains its own copyright and license.

The applicable license depends on the version supplied by the operating
system or host environment.

## 2.4 PyO3

The optional Rust implementation uses PyO3.

PyO3 is an external dependency and retains its own copyright and license.

## 2.5 Rust base64

The optional Rust implementation uses the Rust `base64` crate.

The crate is an external dependency and retains its own copyright and
license.

---

# 3. References Only

The following projects were used as references for implementation,
compatibility, protocol verification, or security analysis.

Reference use does not by itself mean that their source code has been copied
into this project.

## 3.1 Chromium WebUSB

Chromium WebUSB behavior was used as a compatibility reference.

This includes behavior relating to:

- WebUSB API behavior
- Origin and permission handling
- protected USB interfaces
- security-key handling
- transfer behavior
- transfer limits
- device and hotplug behavior
- WebUSB-related errors

The `pyside6-webusb` implementation uses a different architecture based on
PySide6 / QtWebEngine, QWebChannel, pyusb, and libusb.

## 3.2 WebUSB Specification

The WebUSB specification is used as an API and behavior reference.

https://wicg.github.io/webusb/

## 3.3 adb_client

`tth0704/adb_client` was used as a protocol reference for the optional Rust
ADB implementation.

Project:

https://github.com/tth0704/adb_client

The project's ADB implementation was compared during the license audit.

No verbatim source-code match was identified in the compared implementation.

Shared elements are protocol-level information such as:

- command constants
- message field ordering
- protocol structure
- ADB header fields

The `pyside6-webusb` implementation is independently written.

`adb_client` retains its own copyright and license.

If source code from `adb_client` is incorporated in a future version, the
applicable upstream copyright and license notices must be retained.

## 3.4 thegecko/webusb

`thegecko/webusb` was used as a WebUSB implementation reference.

Project:

https://github.com/thegecko/webusb

The project retains its own copyright and license.

No license transfer is implied by reference to the project.

## 3.5 node-usb

`node-usb` was used as an implementation and USB API comparison reference.

Project:

https://github.com/node-usb/node-usb

The project retains its own copyright and license.

No license transfer is implied by reference to the project.

